  { q: 'Can websites see my IP address?', a: 'Yes, every website you visit sees your public IP by necessity, because the server needs it to send responses back to you. That is not a leak, it is how the internet routes traffic. The Best Answer Hub IP Address Checker simply shows you the same address that sites already receive.' },
  { q: 'Is my IP address permanent?', a: 'Usually not. Most home connections use a dynamic IP that can change when you reboot your router or reconnect, rather than a fixed one. A static IP stays the same but is less common for consumers. The Best Answer Hub IP Address Checker shows your current address, which may differ next time.' },
  { q: 'How do I hide or change my IP address?', a: 'A VPN routes your traffic through its server, so sites see the VPN server IP instead of yours, which Cloudflare confirms. Reconnecting can also change a dynamic IP over time. The Best Answer Hub IP Address Checker lets you see your current visible IP, including whether a VPN is already changing it.' },
  { q: 'Does the IP checker store my address?', a: 'No. The Best Answer Hub IP Address Checker shows your public IP and stores nothing about your visit on a server. Your IP is inherently visible to any site you load, but this tool does not log it or build a record; it is a look at the number, not a database entry.' },
  { q: 'Why did IPv4 run out of addresses?', a: 'Because 32 bits only allow about 4.3 billion addresses, and the growth of internet-connected devices exhausted them. The global free pool ran dry on 3 February 2011. IPv6, with its 128-bit addresses, is the long-term fix. The Best Answer Hub IP Address Checker shows which version your connection uses.' },
  { q: 'Should I be worried that a site knows my IP?', a: 'Generally no. Every site needs your IP to respond, and on its own it reveals only your provider and a rough area. It is not your name or address. The Best Answer Hub IP Address Checker exists to replace the worry with understanding, showing exactly what the number does and does not mean.' },
  { q: 'Is the IP Address Checker free?', a: 'Yes. The Best Answer Hub IP Address Checker is completely free with no usage limits and no signup. It stays free because Best Answer Hub is funded by optional paid assessments rather than advertising, so it carries no ads and never upsells a VPN off the back of showing your address.' },
];

